%T A398945 8,0,8,5,1,0,1,1,9,9,5,6,2,4,1,5,4,6,8,6,3,6,3,2,5,5,6,6,3,3,7,4,1,2,
%U A398945 2,0,4,6,3,7,8,3,6,5,5,3,8,6,6,5,7,0,0,9,5,8
%N A398945 Decimal expansion of the large face angle, in radians, of a canonical (dual-uniform) 10-gonal trapezohedron.
%C A398945 The 10-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 10-gonal antiprism.
%C A398945 Its faces are kites with one acute angle (A398944) and three obtuse angles (this constant).
%H A398945 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398945/b398945.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398945 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Decagonal_antitegum">Decagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398945 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%F A398945 Equals arccos(1/2 - cos(Pi/10)) = arccos(1/2 - A019881).
%F A398945 Equals arccos(c), where c = -0.4510... is the smallest root of 16*x^4 - 32*x^3 + 4*x^2 + 12*x + 1.
%e A398945 2.0387450900975860155134391000232068085101199562415...
%t A398945 First[RealDigits[ArcCos[1/2 - Cos[Pi/10]], 10, 100]]
%Y A398945 Cf. A398938 (volume), A398939 (surface area), A398940 (inradius), A398941 (midradius), A398942 (height).
%Y A398945 Cf. A398943 (long edge).
%Y A398945 Cf. A398944 (small face angle), A398946 (dihedral angle).
%Y A398945 Cf. A019881.
%K A398945 nonn,cons,easy
%O A398945 1,1
